 :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8c45b4-79e9-59f1-8aed-0fe57c1e774f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471071} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e759f3-3ea4-52e5-91d5-d81ad7bd1e88" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a389ed-2a90-5310-9d49-d9de078d0e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471073} {:answer/id #uuid "14b87aa4-7616-54b5-993b-17ac7bcfc6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34a389ed-2a90-5310-9d49-d9de078d0e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471073} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bac6d2b-71be-5d31-8a9c-1f6b199802d9" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7a73387-34bf-50c1-bd13-d6c9025be3b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-157470" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $2x-y+z=2$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n- **I.** $Π$ contains the zero-vector\n- **II.** $Π$ is closed under vector addition\n- **III.** $Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **IV.** $Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ 2-2x+y\\end{bmatrix},\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z & =2 \\\\ 2(0)-(0)+(0) & =2 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+0 \\\\ 0+(-2) \\\\ 2+0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z & =2 \\\\ 2(0)-(-2)+(2) & =2 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3018fd-9d16-578f-b050-966890844c9b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Plane Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "700557ce-6572-5ee2-a07f-34d93423cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921864